From abfb8459bcdb4e6ccb2f162820a8aba5c46a2a45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:33:56 +0200
Subject: glm: TF_GLM_PF_QMMF2, block-FP8 prompt GEMMs on qmmf2's 128x64 tile,
 the lane's bytes

Default off. With TF_GLM_PF_QMMF2=1 the lane loads a second image (qmmf2.cu) at boot, and every block-FP8
(FP8G) lane call with at least 256 rows and 1,024 inputs (GLM's prompt o_proj, [q_a | kv_a], q_b, indexer q_b,
shared gate|up, dense layers) runs qmmf2_fp8g<128, 64, 2, 2, 2> instead of qmmf_kernel<FP8G, 64, 64, 1, 4, 4>.
Off, the image is never loaded and matmulOut is unchanged; qmmf.cu is untouched (its SASS is identical).

Bit-exact by construction: per output element the same m16n8k16 bf16 MMA fragments and chains (mma0 at k16
step 0, then 1..3), the same fp32 fma with the column's scale per 64-input group, the same K slices (qmmf.splitK)
summed in the fused kernel's order. Only the schedule changes: 128x64 outputs per CTA on 2x2 warps (64x32 each),
two stages (two CTAs an SM), each group's e4m3 codes widened to bf16 once per warp (byte permute + the same
bf16x2 fma as fp8pair), m16 row tiles walked one at a time, stage copies from addresses computed once. The
running total starts at -0 (no select, 64 fewer live registers at the boundary); -0 + x == x for every non-NaN
x and NaN slice sums are already the canonical 0x7FFFFFFF (FFMA results), proved over all 2^32 inputs on GB10
by tf_qmmf2_neg0_check, which tf-cuda-test lane-pf2 runs.

GB10 at the 1800 MHz cap (bf16 mma peak 87 TFLOPS), 2,048-row halves: o_proj 42 -> 58-63 TFLOPS,
[q_a | kv_a] 41.5 -> 57-62, q_b 40 -> 54-60, shared gate|up 38 -> 50-56.

Tests: tf-cuda-test lane-pf2 (14 shapes x bf16/f32 bytes equal to the lane, 11 taken, special values, strided
rows, odd N, SK 1, tensor scale, 4-mod-8 outputs, the -0 proof); qmmf.zig host test for the plan and names.
gr8 (kindlingai/gr8) was read for its prefill notes only; no gr8 code or design is used here.

